Two overlapping globs list each matched file once, in path order; frontmatter without a `description` prints all its fields, joined by commas.
== args
input/a/**/*
input/**/*
== file input/a/one.md
---
description: One summary.
---
# one
== file input/a/two.md
---
title: Some title
summary: Two summary.
---
== file input/z/three.md
---
description: Three summary.
---
# three
== stdout
glob view: input/a/**/* input/**/*
input/a/one.md (4 lines): description: "One summary."
input/a/two.md (4 lines): title: "Some title", summary: "Two summary."
input/z/three.md (4 lines): description: "Three summary."
== stderr
== exit 0
